			<div class="content" id="post-content-1352604">
									

<p>I changed some adverbs and small grammatical things.</p>
<p>Is anyone else really tired of the illiterate slang of agents and other non-scientific Foundation personnel? I have yet to meet anyone in real life who pronounces &quot;them&quot; &quot;'em&quot;, it's jarring and annoying. These aren't 19th century gold prospectors or 1920s gangsters, they're basically trained soldiers. I can't even tell why it's done, is it to paint these people as somehow gritty and hands-on and too busy or hard for modern conversational conventions or what?</p>

